  Licensed under the MIT License.

What is derived from Claw3D
---------------------------
  * The application stack and structure: Next.js (App Router) + React 19 +
    Three.js + @react-three/fiber + @react-three/drei + Tailwind, and the
    security-header configuration in next.config.ts.
  * The "living 3D virtual office" concept: a navigable office rendered with
    React Three Fiber, populated by procedurally-modelled agent employees
    (capsule body, head, swinging limbs, status halo, floating nameplate) that
    move between desks and a central plaza.

What is original to BINDERY BOX
-------------------------------
  * The business core (packages/): domain, contracts, runtime, data-store,
    policy, connectors, knowledge graph and the Mattermost-mock office adapter,
    together with the Control Plane API (health, workstream, live-log,
    connectors, knowledge search, task run / approval flows).
  * The product framing as an "AI Company-in-a-Box": Mission Control, the Agent
    Performance Market, the Goal Composer, the live operations log overlay and
    the lane-based company simulation.

No secrets, credentials, external-account configuration, or private gateway
integrations from any upstream source were copied into this repository.

